      "number": 1,
      "type": "spike",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "title": "Spike local TTS engine packaging for Windows",
      "description": "Evaluate local-only TTS engines suitable for a packaged Windows Tauri app. Compare CPU/GPU support, model size, license, startup time, audio quality, and integration path. Recommend one engine for basic generation and document extension points for future voice, speed, emotion, and batch options.",
      "gitControl": {
        "enabled": false,
        "branch": "",
        "autoCommit": false,
        "autoPush": false
      },
      "labels": [],
      "roleIds": [],
      "sprintId": "12slsJflpL2jT_nJBM-44",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "rjIFLUuYCN3m7oNKdDxag",
          "text": "Completed the packaging spike document. Recommendation is sherpa-onnx offline TTS as the first Windows-packaged runtime, with comparison against Piper original, OHF piper1-gpl, and Kokoro ONNX plus extension points for voice, speed, emotion, batch, and GPU.\n\nChanged files:\n- docs/tts-engine-spike.md",
